<title>SINGAPORE: India sells Apr Bombay naphtha to Vitol at -$32/T.</title>
<headline>India sells Apr Bombay naphtha to Vitol at -$32/T.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-04-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>State-owned Indian Oil Corp (IOC) has sold by tender 25,000 tonnes of high aromatic naphtha (HAN) lifting April 21-25 to Dutch trader Vitol at $32.00 per tonne below Japanese spot quotes, free-on-board (fob) Bombay on the west coast, industry sources said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The tender closed on April 10 and bids were valid for a day.</p>
<p>IOC's last HAN tender for a cargo lifting March 10-12, was awarded at a much higher level of $25.00 per tonne below Japanese spot quotes on an fob Bombay basis.</p>
<p>-- Singapore Newsroom (+65-8703086)</p>
